


   Rich Rum Sticky Buns
      - adapted from "The New Basics", p.622

   1 recipe not-so-sweet bread dough:   2 C all-purpose flour
                                        1 t salt
                                        1 T wheat germ
        Bread Machine Magic p.123       1 T sugar (or 2)
                                        2 T butter
                                        1 egg + milk to make 7/8 c liquid
                                        
                                     


   filling: 2 T   light brown sugar
            2 T   granulated sugar
            1.5 t ground cinnamon   
            1 c   raisins soaked in rum overnight

   topping: 1/2 c packed light brown sugar
            1/4 c honey
            1/2 c sweet butter (1 stick)
            1/4 c rum (from raisins)

   Melt together topping ingredients and spread
   in a layer on the bottom of a 9 x 13 glass
   baking pan.

   Put filling ingredients in food processor
   and blip a few times to mix and cut up
   raisins.

   Punch down dough and roll out into 12 x 16
   inch rectangle or something like that.
   Maybe 16 x 16 be better.

   Spread filling over dough and press it into
   dough with rolling pin.  Roll as tightly as
   possible into cylinder.  Using dental floss,
   cut cylinder into 15 equal pieces.  Place on
   top of topping in pan. 

   Let rise until-double-in-bulk and bake for
   25-30 minutes at 350.  Let cool 5 minutes
   and invert on to serving plate.
